sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User / Terminal
    participant App as SysGuard C++ App (DriverClient)
    participant VFS as Linux VFS Subsystem
    participant Driver as sysguard.ko (/dev/sysguard)
    participant Kernel as Linux Kernel Core

    User->>App: Launch SysGuard / Query Driver Status
    App->>VFS: open("/dev/sysguard", O_RDWR)
    VFS->>Driver: sysguard_open()
    Driver-->>VFS: Success (fd allocated)
    VFS-->>App: fd = 3

    Note over App,Driver: IOCTL: Query Driver Status
    App->>VFS: ioctl(fd, SYSGUARD_IOCTL_GET_STATUS, &status)
    VFS->>Driver: sysguard_ioctl(SYSGUARD_IOCTL_GET_STATUS)
    Driver->>Driver: Populate sysguard_status struct
    Driver->>VFS: copy_to_user(&status, sizeof(status))
    VFS-->>App: Return 0 (Success)

    Note over App,Driver: IOCTL: Query Kernel Telemetry
    App->>VFS: ioctl(fd, SYSGUARD_IOCTL_GET_KERNEL_INFO, &kinfo)
    VFS->>Driver: sysguard_ioctl(SYSGUARD_IOCTL_GET_KERNEL_INFO)
    Driver->>Kernel: si_meminfo(&si), ktime_get_boottime_seconds()
    Kernel-->>Driver: Memory stats & boot duration
    Driver->>VFS: copy_to_user(&kinfo, sizeof(kinfo))
    VFS-->>App: Return 0 (Success)

    Note over App,Driver: Read Operation
    App->>VFS: read(fd, buffer, 1024)
    VFS->>Driver: sysguard_read()
    Driver->>VFS: copy_to_user(buffer, diagnostic_text)
    VFS-->>App: Return bytes read

    App->>VFS: close(fd)
    VFS->>Driver: sysguard_release()
    Driver-->>VFS: Closed
    App-->>User: Render formatted metrics on Dashboard
